From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:09:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add provider family execution allowlist

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: expose and enforce provider-family execution allowlist
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-provider-policy
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Add a provider-family execution allowlist that gates model switching,
persisted routes, dispatch, and failover. Empty or absent means unrestricted;
a non-empty list fails closed for unknown identities.

Why it exists:
Keeps sessions inside explicit provider allowlists while preserving empty-list
legacy behavior. Non-goal is restricting picker visibility only; the picker
narrowing is a separate config field that cannot grant execution the allowlist
denies.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs adds the allowed_providers field.
crates/jcode-provider-core/src/lib.rs defines ProviderFamily, ProviderFamilyPolicy,
provider_family() methods on RuntimeKey and ModelRouteApiMethod.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/mod.rs enforces policy in set_model and route filtering.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/dispatch.rs and multi_provider.rs enforce in failover.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/catalog_routes.rs filters catalog routes by policy.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/tests.rs covers policy enforcement.
crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs documents the policy.

Update guidance:
Keep ProviderFamily taxonomy exhaustive. OpenRouterEu is a forward-compatible
variant that the OpenRouter EU patch maps a runtime to. The policy must fail
closed for unknown entries and preserve empty-list legacy behavior.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-base provider_route_ --lib
